# Responsive UI Conventions

## WindowSize Breakpoints (Material3)

```kotlin
enum class WindowSize { COMPACT, MEDIUM, EXPANDED }

// Breakpoints (in ScreenDimens.windowSize getter):
// COMPACT:  < 600dp  (phones)
// MEDIUM:   600-839dp (foldables, small tablets)
// EXPANDED: >= 840dp  (tablets, desktop)
```

## ScreenDimens (via CompositionLocal)

```kotlin
val dimens = LocalDimens.current

dimens.windowSize          // COMPACT, MEDIUM, EXPANDED
dimens.isCompact           // Boolean shorthand
dimens.screenWidth         // Dp
dimens.screenHeight        // Dp
dimens.isLandscape         // Boolean

// Responsive helpers
dimens.responsiveDp(compact = 16.dp, medium = 24.dp, expanded = 32.dp)
dimens.responsiveColumns() // 1, 2, or 3
dimens.widthPercent(80f)   // 80% of screen width as Dp
```

Access via `LocalDimens.current` anywhere inside `MezonTheme`.

## Scaled Typography

3 pre-built `Typography` objects — selected by `WindowSize`:

| Style | Compact | Medium | Expanded |
|-------|---------|--------|----------|
| bodyLarge | 16sp | 17sp | 18sp |
| bodyMedium | 14sp | 15sp | 16sp |
| bodySmall | 12sp | 13sp | 14sp |
| titleMedium | 16sp | 17sp | 18sp |
| titleSmall | 14sp | 15sp | 16sp |
| labelSmall | 11sp | 12sp | 13sp |

Scale is deliberately subtle (+1-2sp) — chat apps should not scale text dramatically.

```kotlin
fun scaledTypography(dimens: ScreenDimens): Typography = when (dimens.windowSize) {
    WindowSize.COMPACT -> CompactTypography
    WindowSize.MEDIUM -> MediumTypography
    WindowSize.EXPANDED -> ExpandedTypography
}
```

Typography is provided automatically by `MezonTheme` — use `MaterialTheme.typography.*` in composables.

## Dimens Object (Fixed Tokens)

`Dimens` provides fixed dimension tokens used across the app:

```kotlin
object Dimens {
    val avatarSmall = 24.dp    // Inline mentions
    val avatarMedium = 32.dp   // Chat bubbles
    val avatarLarge = 48.dp    // DM list items
    val paddingSmall = 8.dp
    val paddingMedium = 12.dp
    val paddingDefault = 16.dp
    val cornerMedium = 8.dp
    val bubbleMaxWidth = 320.dp
    // ... etc
}
```

These are NOT responsive — they are consistent across all screen sizes. Use `dimens.responsiveDp()` for values that should change per breakpoint.

## Rules

- Always use `MaterialTheme.typography.*` — never hardcode `fontSize` in composables
- Use `Dimens.*` for consistent spacing/sizing tokens
- Use `LocalDimens.current.responsiveDp()` only when layout genuinely needs breakpoint adaptation (e.g. form max-width on login screen)
- `bubbleMaxWidth = 320.dp` is fixed intentionally — matches Telegram/WhatsApp behavior
- Typography objects are top-level private vals — zero per-composition allocation
- `rememberScreenDimens()` is called once in `MezonTheme` — don't call it in child composables
